            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-97031",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-97031"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-97031?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.26.9",
              "help": {
                "text": "Multiple ECH outer extension references are not permitted under RFC 9849; previously, a client could send a well-crafted packet that could trigger memory exhaustion in the server process by specifying multiple references.\n\nWe now reject these as malformed and curb the memory amplification vector as a result.\n",
                "markdown": "> Multiple ECH outer extension references are not permitted under RFC 9849; previously, a client could send a well-crafted packet that could trigger memory exhaustion in the server process by specifying multiple references.\n\nWe now reject these as malformed and curb the memory amplification vector as a result.\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.26.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.26.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.26.9                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
                "affected_version": ">=1.27.0-0,<1.27.2",
