            {
              "id": "CVE-2026-56857",
              "name": "OsPackageVulnerability",
              "shortDescription": {
                "text": "CVE-2026-56857"
              },
              "helpUri": "https://scout.docker.com/v/CVE-2026-56857?s=golang&n=stdlib&t=golang&vr=%3C1.26.9",
              "help": {
                "text": "On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).\n",
                "markdown": "> On Windows, when the target of Root.Mkdir or Root.MkdirAll is a junction pointing to an empty location, the operation can create a directory at the junction target even when that target is located outside the root. This only applies to operations where the last path component is a junction (path/to/junction, but not path/junction/target).\n\n|                                          |\n|Package         pkg:golang/stdlib@1.26.6  |\n|Affected range  <1.26.9                   |\n|Fixed version   1.26.9                    |\n"
              },
              "properties": {
